{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"118870","commit":"10e555f37ea06b24e0fabcf70a01b7f8461a45a3","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The addition of `ReplaceCaseWithInsensitiveMatch` to the list of operators in `LogicalPlanOptimizer` is correct, but given the issues mentioned above with the logic in `matchesCase`, this rule may not work as intended and could lead to incorrect query results. Ensure that the logic in `matchesCase` is corrected before relying on this optimization.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java--10491:10528","promptId":"#CDZ3F","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":10491,"endPos":10528,"startLine":179,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":179,"endLineOffset":49,"length":38}]}]},{"comment":"The `ChangeCase` class introduces a new enum `Case` with methods `process` and `matchesCase`. The `matchesCase` method checks if the string is entirely in uppercase or lowercase. However, this logic might not be accurate for all locales, especially those with special casing rules (e.g., Turkish locale where \u0027i\u0027 -\u003e \u0027İ\u0027 and \u0027I\u0027 -\u003e \u0027ı\u0027). Consider using `String.toUpperCase(Locale)` and `String.toLowerCase(Locale)` to compare strings in a locale-sensitive manner.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/scalar/string/ToUpper.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/scalar/string/ToUpper.java-2429:2443,2469:2488-1742:1747,1764:1774","promptId":"#7SCP4","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack